WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.000
What's going on?

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.520
Even if you get five coins, 
these battles don't end?

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:11.030
Five coins isn't the win condition?

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:12.920
Shock.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:14.160
What does this mean?

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:15.950
No...

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:19.000
If it doesn't end after you get five coins,

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.660
then how can I get Chi-chan's memories back?

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.110
Tama?!

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:10.020
Where am I?

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:19.670
This is... Mayu's room?

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:22.490
Yes, this is the room of white windows.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:25.000
Who are you?

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:31.860
Shiro.

00:02:32.990 --> 00:02:34.110
Kuro is here, too.

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:35.680
The ones who left.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:38.470
I know this voice!

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.820
The door will open soon.

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:43.940
The door...

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.590
The door will...

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.040
What is this?

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:52.110
Let me go!

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:53.970
Hey, let me go!

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:56.260
<i>The girl of the beginning has returned.</i>

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:57.290
<i>The keyhole.</i>

00:02:57.290 --> 00:03:00.400
No! No! No!

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:14.900
Now all I need is the key...

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:16.880
I wonder how this will go.

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:20.540
There are five Selectors left in the game.

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:22.340
It's almost time for the climax.

00:03:23.410 --> 00:03:25.960
I need to make the game more interesting.

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:29.190
Isn't that right, Eternal?

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:36.440
<b>Ruuko</b>

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.000
Where did you go, Tama?

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:53.800
<i>That message from Mizushima-san...</i>

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:57.920
<i>If getting five coins isn't how you win,</i>

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:01.500
<i>does that mean there's no 
way to recover lost memories?</i>

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:08.920
Correct. We haven't been told how to win.

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:14.720
But we were told that if we win, it will be 
possible in the end to alter memories.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:19.020
Which means that to win this time, 
you have to do something different?

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:20.220
Probably.

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:26.410
That message from Mizushima-san...
If getting five coins isn't how you win,
does that mean there's no way
to recover lost memories?

00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:26.410
<i>We don't know how to win yet,</i>

00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:31.370
<i>but I'll keep winning battles and 
get your memories back, Chi-chan.</i>

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:32.290
That message from Mizushima-san...
If getting five coins isn't how you win,
does that mean there's no way
to recover lost memories?

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:33.210
We don't know how to win yet,
but I'll keep winning battles and
get your memories back, Chi-chan.

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:39.750
<b>Unknown Caller</b>

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:45.220
Yes?

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:46.840
<i>Hi there.</i>

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:49.640
Carnival...

00:04:52.230 --> 00:04:54.200
Tama-chan's gone?

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:57.030
I didn't see it happen, either...

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:58.480
But why?

00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:00.840
This is just a guess,

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:03.040
but Tama is a special LRIG,

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:06.320
so she may have been caught 
up in something big.

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:09.240
What's going on?

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:10.810
I don't know.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:14.370
But it looks like what's happening 
here is totally different

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:17.210
than the Selector battles we know.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:25.220
That message from Mizushima-san...
If getting five coins isn't how you win,
does that mean there's no way
to recover lost memories?

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:25.220
We don't know how to win yet,
but I'll keep winning battles and
get your memories back, Chi-chan.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:25.220
Thanks.
I believe in you, Suzu.

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:30.430
Oh, hey!

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:34.680
How've you been?

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:41.600
I'm sorry, who are you again?

00:05:42.310 --> 00:05:45.400
So you forgot about me, huh?

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:47.920
Is it because you lost your coins?

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:52.330
Can you tell me more about that?

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:01.350
How are you enjoying this 
round of Selector battles?

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:03.380
Having fun?

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:08.050
These battles could never be fun.

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:11.640
Is all of this your doing?

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:13.910
It was Eternal who set it up.

00:06:13.910 --> 00:06:14.950
Eternal?

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:17.330
The Room of White Windows itself.

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:23.480
The goal of these new battles is for 
Eternal to pick itself a new master.

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:25.320
You can't be serious...

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:29.090
The Room of White Windows 
summoned me personally

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:33.480
and gave me more information 
than the other Selectors.

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:36.580
Looks like it wants me to mix things up.

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:42.040
Why are you telling me this?

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:46.000
You're the only Selector who defeated me.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:49.010
If you're not taking this seriously, 
it's not worth defeating you.

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:51.690
So I'm doing you a special favor.

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:58.670
There's a lot of stuff I forgot, too.

00:06:58.670 --> 00:07:00.560
You were a Selector, too?

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:01.760
That's right.

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:07.280
When I was in trouble, 
you told me about Satomi-oniichan.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:11.860
And Satomi-oniichan found 
me someone to fight.

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:12.540
Satomi...

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:14.760
Then, when I had one coin left...

00:07:19.930 --> 00:07:22.130
Hey, are you okay?

00:07:23.490 --> 00:07:25.980
What did I do?

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:29.660
I'm going to become the master of that room,

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:32.760
and make the world a lot more fun.

00:07:33.310 --> 00:07:35.120
A world where the battles never end,

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:37.720
and their outcome determines everything.

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:41.560
A world where the battles 
go on for eternity...

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:43.950
What could be better?

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:49.480
If you became the master of the room,

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:51.820
could you get other Selectors' memories back?

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:56.330
It was the master of the room who 
invented the battles for memories.

00:07:56.900 --> 00:08:00.330
They can probably do whatever they like 
with the memories that were stolen.

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:02.810
If you want to make your wish come true,

00:08:02.810 --> 00:08:06.880
you'll have to defeat all 
the remaining Selectors.

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:11.890
I gave you the information.

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:14.210
Now get to work.

00:08:14.210 --> 00:08:16.550
Right now, it's not even worth fighting you.

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:19.760
If you want to make your wish come true,

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:23.260
you'll have to defeat all 
the remaining Selectors.

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:35.860
When I was Layla's LRIG,
I saw someone named Carnival.

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:41.330
They had information about the battles 
that Selectors aren't supposed to know.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:44.710
And you think they might know about Tama?

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:46.500
Yes, maybe.

00:08:48.450 --> 00:08:49.800
This is the place.

00:08:58.180 --> 00:08:59.860
Are you Kominato Ruuko?

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:04.460
Who are you?

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:09.230
That's him! Carnival!

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:11.570
You need something from me?

00:09:13.270 --> 00:09:15.320
Do you know an LRIG named Tama?

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:19.480
Oh, I just heard that name.

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:21.330
What do you mean?

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:25.710
A Selector I just fought called 
her LRIG by that name.

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:28.420
She should still be close.

00:09:28.670 --> 00:09:33.380
I believe her name was... Homura Suzuko.

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:36.130
Homura Suzuko?

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:46.940
They can probably do whatever they like 
with the memories that were stolen.

00:09:47.340 --> 00:09:49.330
If you want to make your wish come true,

00:09:49.330 --> 00:09:52.400
you'll have to defeat all 
the remaining Selectors.

00:09:58.520 --> 00:10:04.720
Homura Suzuko said there's a reason she 
has to win the battles, no matter what.

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:08.660
<i>And she stole Tama for that reason?</i>

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:16.540
I'm going to get Chi-chan's memories back.

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:18.240
No matter what.

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:21.980
When humans get too attached to something,

00:10:21.980 --> 00:10:23.680
it narrows their field of vision.

00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:29.360
This should be a pretty 
interesting development.

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:39.540
<i>I hope I can find some kind of clue...</i>

00:10:44.850 --> 00:10:45.870
<i>Confirmation.</i>

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:48.710
<i>Is Kurebayashi-san back?</i>

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:54.880
Sorry.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:56.640
It looks like she's left already.

00:10:57.600 --> 00:10:59.340
She's near the street up ahead.

00:10:59.590 --> 00:11:00.840
Got it!

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:15.350
Excuse me...

00:11:15.350 --> 00:11:18.080
You're Kurebayashi-kun's friend, aren't you?

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:19.400
Yes...

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:21.830
Is she still sick?

00:11:21.830 --> 00:11:23.780
Yeah, kind of...

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:26.440
We can't get a hold of her on the phone.

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:28.020
Do you know what's going on with her?

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:29.040
Um...

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:31.340
Could you tell her to call us?

00:11:31.340 --> 00:11:32.060
Discovery.

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:33.500
There you are.

00:11:33.940 --> 00:11:34.850
Late.

00:11:34.850 --> 00:11:37.190
If we don't hurry, we won't 
make it in time for the movie.

00:11:37.190 --> 00:11:40.970
The movie? Wait... Huh?

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:45.160
I-I'm sorry... I think you have the wrong person.

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:46.600
I'm not going to any movies.

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:47.640
Blunt.

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:49.020
You're a Selector, aren't you?

00:11:54.130 --> 00:11:56.270
Are you also a Selector, Hanna-san?

00:11:56.500 --> 00:11:57.690
Affirmation.

00:11:57.690 --> 00:11:58.850
Hypothesis.

00:11:58.850 --> 00:12:01.150
Yuzuki-san is missing work because

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:03.740
she was caught up in the 
Selector battles, right?

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:06.070
That's right.

00:12:06.070 --> 00:12:07.640
Trade.

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:10.830
All right, Uemura-san, let's trade information.

00:12:11.590 --> 00:12:14.150
We need allies.

00:12:14.820 --> 00:12:16.840
I'd love to!

00:12:21.610 --> 00:12:22.380
She's close.

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:23.510
Where?

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:25.300
That way!

00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:29.720
<b>Egg Tart</b>

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:32.230
Yuzuki, which one is she?

00:12:32.230 --> 00:12:35.650
I'm sorry. There are so many 
people that I can't tell.

00:12:49.640 --> 00:12:50.740
Understanding.

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:53.530
Your friend's LRIG is missing.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:55.030
Unfortunately,

00:12:55.030 --> 00:12:58.200
I have no information on 
similar events occurring.

00:12:58.200 --> 00:12:59.340
I see.

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:00.770
Shock.

00:13:00.770 --> 00:13:02.660
I'm very surprised, though.

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:09.660
So you're friends with the legendary Selector 
Kiyoi-san told me about, Kominato Ruuko-san.

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:12.270
Ruuko's just a normal girl.

00:13:14.220 --> 00:13:15.110
Hunch.

00:13:15.110 --> 00:13:18.970
I think something strange is going on 
with these latest Selector battles.

00:13:19.830 --> 00:13:21.030
Something...

00:13:22.930 --> 00:13:25.840
I couldn't say anything about that.

00:13:25.840 --> 00:13:29.440
But we need to stop that Carnival person.

00:13:30.180 --> 00:13:31.580
I do agree with that.

00:13:32.020 --> 00:13:32.930
Suggestion.

00:13:33.440 --> 00:13:37.290
Then let's go meet my ally now.

00:13:42.520 --> 00:13:44.720
Yeah, I'm sure of it.

00:13:44.720 --> 00:13:45.670
She's on the platform.

00:13:45.890 --> 00:13:46.960
Got it.

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:53.680
<i>The train will be arriving 
shortly on track 1.</i>

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:55.810
<b>Hanazono
Shrine</b>

00:13:58.200 --> 00:13:59.770
Here I am.

00:14:03.080 --> 00:14:04.320
I see.

00:14:04.710 --> 00:14:07.780
So you're Kominato Ruuko-san's friend.

00:14:08.440 --> 00:14:09.240
Coincidence.

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:10.640
You know her?

00:14:11.130 --> 00:14:14.040
When I was Aoi Akira's LRIG,

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:15.860
we battled once.

00:14:20.770 --> 00:14:22.540
I remember you...

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:23.430
Understanding.

00:14:23.430 --> 00:14:24.810
That's a bit of a curve ball,

00:14:24.810 --> 00:14:27.320
but you've met before, I see.

00:14:27.320 --> 00:14:29.590
Well, then, I'll introduce you again.

00:14:30.170 --> 00:14:32.600
This is one of my allies,

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:34.140
Mizushima Kiyoi-san.

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:35.060
Mizushima...

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:38.520
Then you're the person who 
gave that invitation to Ruuko.

00:14:38.840 --> 00:14:42.260
Ruuko called you yesterday, actually.

00:14:43.260 --> 00:14:45.190
I see.

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:47.610
I'm sorry. I was kind of busy yesterday.

00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:51.410
Does that mean Kominato-san's 
involved in these battles, as well?

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:52.550
Yes.

00:14:52.550 --> 00:14:55.490
Then I'd like to ask for her help once more.

00:14:55.720 --> 00:14:57.830
Naturally. That makes sense.

00:14:57.830 --> 00:15:01.480
But she's busy finding Tama-chan now...

00:15:01.480 --> 00:15:03.460
That's Ruuko's LRIG.

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:05.840
And she suddenly vanished...

00:15:06.640 --> 00:15:07.650
Cooperation.

00:15:07.650 --> 00:15:12.910
I think we could resolve that 
faster if we all worked together.

00:15:12.910 --> 00:15:13.800
That's right.

00:15:14.090 --> 00:15:15.010
Suggestion.

00:15:15.010 --> 00:15:19.320
Why don't we contact 
Kominato-san immediately?

00:15:19.320 --> 00:15:20.690
Yes.

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:26.710
<i>Ruuko, hey...</i>

00:15:26.710 --> 00:15:27.800
Hitoe, sorry.

00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:29.740
I'm a little busy now.

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:32.700
I might be able to get Tama back.

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:34.550
Really?

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:36.070
Yeah...

00:15:36.860 --> 00:15:37.660
Yeah.

00:15:38.680 --> 00:15:42.710
Ruuko says she's following the 
Selector who stole Tama-chan.

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:43.420
Who?

00:15:44.030 --> 00:15:46.450
She said her name is Homura Suzuko.

00:15:46.450 --> 00:15:47.660
Stop her!

00:15:47.660 --> 00:15:50.320
Homura Suzuko-san is on our side.

00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:52.420
She wouldn't steal anyone's LRIG.

00:15:52.420 --> 00:15:53.640
Ruuko!

00:15:54.310 --> 00:15:55.880
She's getting on the train.

00:15:54.660 --> 00:15:55.880
<i>Ruuko!</i>

00:15:55.880 --> 00:15:58.100
Sorry, I'm getting on a train, so I'm hanging up.

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:00.210
<i>I'll call you back.</i>

00:16:00.210 --> 00:16:01.380
Ruuko, wait!

00:16:05.010 --> 00:16:06.610
It's no good. I can't get through.

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:07.570
Roger.

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:09.400
I'll call Suzuko-san.

00:16:11.150 --> 00:16:11.860
Failed.

00:16:11.860 --> 00:16:13.320
Her voice mail picks up.

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:14.560
What do we do?

00:16:14.560 --> 00:16:15.300
Impede.

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:17.070
We need to stop her somehow.

00:16:17.070 --> 00:16:19.770
But we don't know which train she's on,

00:16:19.770 --> 00:16:21.380
or how to find her...

00:16:21.850 --> 00:16:23.040
Uncertainty...

00:16:28.180 --> 00:16:31.870
<i>At a time when we need to fight Carnival,</i>

00:16:31.870 --> 00:16:34.460
<i>we can't let the two of them fight.</i>

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:36.970
<i>What do we do?</i>

00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:38.930
<i>How can we stop them?</i>

00:16:39.270 --> 00:16:40.890
<i>What can we do?</i>

00:16:40.890 --> 00:16:42.940
<i>We don't have enough information...</i>

00:16:46.870 --> 00:16:48.310
The other.

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:50.820
The other girl.

00:16:58.940 --> 00:17:02.080
Is this... the Room of White Windows?

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:03.460
The other girl.

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:05.480
I've been waiting.

00:17:05.480 --> 00:17:06.330
Who's there?

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:08.010
I've been waiting.

00:17:08.010 --> 00:17:09.410
I am Eternal.

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:10.400
Eternal?

00:17:10.990 --> 00:17:12.550
Open the door.

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:15.300
Open the lock...

00:17:16.230 --> 00:17:17.890
Who will win?

00:17:18.530 --> 00:17:20.510
Who is the weak one?

00:17:20.960 --> 00:17:22.170
Battle.

00:17:22.170 --> 00:17:24.360
Battle, and risk your life.

00:17:24.360 --> 00:17:26.320
Choose. You must do it.

00:17:26.950 --> 00:17:29.200
Find the key.

00:17:29.200 --> 00:17:30.300
The answer.

00:17:30.300 --> 00:17:31.730
The law.

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:35.200
Me.

00:17:37.600 --> 00:17:38.790
Find...

00:17:41.500 --> 00:17:42.950
the key?

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:48.900
You?

00:17:51.310 --> 00:17:52.290
Kiyoi-san!

00:17:52.290 --> 00:17:53.650
Mizushima-san!

00:17:58.000 --> 00:17:59.400
Are you okay?

00:17:59.400 --> 00:18:00.240
Concern.

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:02.430
You just passed out...

00:18:02.430 --> 00:18:03.880
I'm fine.

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:06.930
And I know where they are.

00:18:06.930 --> 00:18:08.390
Let's go get them.

00:18:08.580 --> 00:18:09.810
Kiyoi-san?

00:18:09.810 --> 00:18:11.610
We'll talk later.

00:18:12.670 --> 00:18:14.680
Mizushima Kiyoi...

00:18:14.680 --> 00:18:17.610
So now she's been chosen?

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:22.770
I guess I'm just another pawn, too.

00:18:23.270 --> 00:18:24.940
This will be fun.

00:18:30.910 --> 00:18:33.250
<i>I'll get Tama back, no matter what.</i>

00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:36.970
<i>I decided I'd never be apart from her again.</i>

00:18:37.400 --> 00:18:38.500
Yuzuki...

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:41.220
It's so crowded that it's hard to tell,

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:44.000
but I'm sure she's on this train.

00:18:44.460 --> 00:18:45.680
I'll know if you get close.

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:11.670
She's close. She's in this car.

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:16.710
<b>Ikebukuro</b>

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:16.710
<i>The train will be arriving 
shortly on track 7...</i>

00:19:25.270 --> 00:19:25.990
Here you go.

00:19:25.990 --> 00:19:27.140
Thank you!

00:19:27.140 --> 00:19:29.030
Ruuko, she got off the train.

00:19:29.030 --> 00:19:29.730
Get off, quick!

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:35.110
There she is! That girl!

00:19:35.450 --> 00:19:37.350
The one who just went down the stairs!

00:19:40.960 --> 00:19:43.200
They should be in this area.

00:19:58.870 --> 00:20:01.280
Homura Suzuko-san...

00:20:08.010 --> 00:20:10.100
Who are you?

00:20:14.010 --> 00:20:15.530
Give back Tama.

00:20:15.530 --> 00:20:17.070
What are you talking about?

00:20:17.600 --> 00:20:18.650
Don't play dumb.

00:20:19.830 --> 00:20:22.280
Suzuko, she's a Selector.

00:20:26.160 --> 00:20:29.690
<i>You'll have to defeat all 
the remaining Selectors.</i>

00:20:33.020 --> 00:20:35.540
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:39.090
But if you're a Selector...

00:20:39.720 --> 00:20:41.550
I have to beat you!

00:20:45.590 --> 00:20:48.140
Homura Suzuko, the one who defeated me,

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:50.720
and Kominato Ruuko, 
the one who released Mayu.

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:52.520
This is a good match I set up.

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:55.480
Which one will win?

00:20:55.480 --> 00:20:56.850
What did you say?!

00:20:58.700 --> 00:20:59.770
I didn't see you there.

00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:01.040
You asshole!

00:21:01.040 --> 00:21:03.320
I'm the one who gets to fight Kominato Ruuko!

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:05.600
She's my prey!

00:21:05.600 --> 00:21:07.400
The situation's changed.

00:21:07.400 --> 00:21:08.590
Give up.

00:21:08.590 --> 00:21:12.040
And there's no way you 
can beat Kominato Ruuko.

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:12.950
What?!

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:16.830
Shut the hell up!

00:21:16.830 --> 00:21:18.620
Fight me!

00:21:18.620 --> 00:21:20.550
I'll take you down first!

00:21:31.530 --> 00:21:32.640
Over there!

00:21:46.480 --> 00:21:47.110
Open!

00:21:47.110 --> 00:21:48.180
Open!

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:56.040
Contact / Key and Keyhole

00:23:26.760 --> 00:23:29.050
I can't beat her with anything 
less than my full strength.

00:23:29.050 --> 00:23:30.120
Suzu is amazing...

00:23:30.120 --> 00:23:32.200
That smirk of yours pisses me off.

00:23:32.200 --> 00:23:33.620
Who is Eternal?

00:23:33.620 --> 00:23:35.750
We all have a reason why we battle.

00:23:35.750 --> 00:23:38.760
This is an audition for you all.

00:23:37.890 --> 00:23:41.060
The Eve / Trust and Betrayal

00:23:38.760 --> 00:23:41.060
"The Eve / Trust and Betrayal."
